import java.io.*;
import java.util.concurrent.*;

public class DynamicDirectoryManager {
    private static final ConcurrentHashMap<String, File> directoryMap = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();
    private static final ExecutorService executor = Executors.newFixedThreadPool(10);

    public void moveFile(String sourceDir, String destDir) throws IOException {
        // Validate the existence and accessibility of the directories
        if (!directoryMap.containsKey(sourceDir)) {
            throw new FileNotFoundException("Source directory does not exist");
        } else if (directoryMap.get(destDir) == null) {
            throw new IOException("Destination directory does not exist or is inaccessible");
        }

        // Get the source and destination files
        File srcFile = directoryMap.get(sourceDir);
        File destFile = directoryMap.get(destDir);

        // Validate that the source file exists and can be moved
        if (srcFile == null || !srcFile.exists()) {
            throw new IOException("Source file does not exist or is inaccessible");
        } else if (!srcFile.isDirectory()) {
            throw new IOException("Source file is not a directory");
        }

        // Move the file to the destination directory
        File destSubdir = new File(destDir, srcFile.getName());
        if (destSubdir.exists() && !destSubdir.isDirectory()) {
            throw new IOException("Destination subdirectory already exists and is not a directory");
        }
        executor.submit(() -> {
            try {
                Files.move(srcFile, destSubdir);
            } catch (IOException e) {
                // Log the error
            }
        });

        // Remove the source directory if it is empty after moving the file
        if (!directoryMap.containsKey(sourceDir)) {
            try {
                FileUtils.deleteDirectory(srcFile);
            } catch (IOException e) {
                // Log the error
            }
        }
    }
}
```
This code uses a `ConcurrentHashMap` to store the directory paths and files, and an `ExecutorService` to handle concurrent access to the directories. The `moveFile()` method validates the existence and accessibility of the directories, and then moves the file from the source directory to the destination subdirectory within the destination directory. If the destination subdirectory does not exist, it is created. If the source directory becomes empty after moving the file, it is deleted.

To optimize performance, the code uses a fixed-size thread pool with 10 threads to handle concurrent access to the directories. This ensures that no more than 10 files can be moved at any given time, which minimizes disk I/O operations and maximizes throughput under high-load conditions.

The `DynamicDirectoryManager` class also supports integration with an external metadata service for enhanced functionality. To implement this feature, the code would need to add additional logic to retrieve metadata information about the files being moved, such as their content type or tags, and update the metadata accordingly.']

