The function `delete` removes a profile from the cache given its ID.

The function `insert` inserts a new profile into the cache, updating the cache size if necessary. It also performs garbage collection to remove any expired profiles from the cache.

The function `thread_function` is responsible for managing user profiles and fetching external data in a separate thread. It randomly selects a profile ID from the cache, retrieves the corresponding profile, and updates the cache with new data if necessary. If an external API call fails, it falls back on cached data if available, or returns an empty profile if no data is available. The function also handles garbage collection to remove any expired profiles from the cache.

The main function initializes the cache with a default size and inserts some initial profiles into the cache. It then creates 10 threads that manage user profiles and fetch external data concurrently, using the `thread_function` as a thread entry point. Finally, the main function waits for all threads to finish before exiting.']

