The `client_cache_get()` and `central_cache_put()` functions are thread-safe because they use atomic operations to update the priority values of the items in the cache. The `evict_cache()` function is also thread-safe because it uses a critical section to prevent concurrent access to the cache.

This implementation has some limitations. For example, it does not handle item expiration, which means that items are removed from the cache only when they are explicitly evicted by calling the `evict_cache()` function. It also assumes that the client cache is always used in a multi-threaded environment, which may not be the case for all applications. However, this implementation demonstrates the basic principles of caching and provides a good starting point for further development.']

