#### 3.2.5 Summary

In this section, we discussed the use of dynamic arrays in C programming language to store a large number of elements. We introduced three types of dynamic arrays: fixed-size array, linked list, and array of structures. The fixed-size array is the most common and simple implementation, while the linked list provides more flexibility but requires more memory for nodes. Finally, we discussed the array of structures and array of pairs that provide a way to store two elements in a single data structure.

In summary, dynamic arrays are useful when you need to store an unknown number of elements, as they can grow or shrink dynamically based on user input. By choosing the appropriate type of dynamic array, you can optimize memory usage and improve performance in your C program.']

