We have also defined a `validate_payload_size` function to validate the MAC payload size of a frame. This function checks if the payload size is valid by checking if it is between 46 and 1500 bytes (inclusive). If the payload size is not valid, the function returns false.

We have also defined a `validate_payload` function to validate the MAC payload data of a frame. This function checks if the payload data is valid by calculating the checksum of the payload data and comparing it to the checksum in the payload data. If the calculated checksum does not match the checksum in the payload data, the function returns false.

