The functions are designed to be efficient in terms of memory usage and re-allocation overhead when handling large datasets. They also support concurrent updates from multiple threads without data corruption, using read-write locks to manage lock contention. The `Statistics` structure is designed to be easily extendable to support additional statistical metrics in the future.

