To optimize memory usage and minimize fragmentation, this implementation uses a linked list instead of a dynamic array for memory allocation and access patterns. This allows for efficient insertion and deletion of entries at the beginning or end of the list without having to reallocate memory for the entire list. The `numEntries` variable keeps track of the number of entries in the list, which can be used to efficiently manage memory usage under varying load conditions.

