The code also includes error handling mechanisms to manage scenarios where the integer list is empty or when memory allocation fails, ensuring robust memory allocation strategies that minimize leaks and optimize performance. Developers must balance efficiency and readability while considering the impact of bitwise operations on execution speed, as well as the need for efficient memory management during peak usage to prevent resource exhaustion.

