The function `addRecord` takes a pointer to a linked list, an integer argument `rnti`, a character argument `crcIndicationRel8Tag`, and an integer argument `additionalIntegerField`. It adds a new record to the end of the linked list by appending it to the existing records. If the number of records in the list exceeds its capacity, it resizes the linked list by doubling its capacity using `realloc`. If allocation fails, it prints an error message using `perror` and exits with a non-zero status code.

The function `findLargestInt` takes a pointer to a linked list as its argument and finds the largest integer among records in the list. It uses a loop to iterate through the records in the linked list and checks if each record's additional integer field is larger than the current largest integer found so far. If a record has an additional integer field that is larger than the current largest integer, it updates the largest integer to that value. After looping through all records in the linked list, it prints the largest integer using `printf`.

